WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:05.534
♪♪

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:09.033
Narrator:
WHEN YOU'RE SITTING OUTDOORS
AND IT STARTS GETTING CHILLY,

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.467
YOU CAN SHIVER, PUT ON MORE
LAYERS OF CLOTHING,

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.501
OR PRESS A BUTTON
TO LET THE FURNITURE

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:15.667
YOU'RE SITTING ON
WARM YOU UP.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.968
DESIGNED FOR USE
IN THE OUTDOORS,

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.801
AND IN COLDER INDOOR SPACES,

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:23.133
HEATED FURNITURE
IS A HOT NEW TREND.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:28.167
THIS HEATED LOUNGE
IS HIP AND PRACTICAL.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.667
DISCREET DRAIN HOLES PREVENT
RAIN WATER FROM PUDDLING,

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.300
AND THE EASY-TO-REACH
HEAT CONTROL KNOB

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.300
IS LOCATED UNDERNEATH THE SEAT.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.000
BENCHES, MULTI-SEAT LOUNGES,
AND SINGLE CHAIRS

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.133
CAN ALL BE MADE INTO
HEATED FURNITURE.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:47.033
THE FIRST STEP
IS TO COAT A FIBERGLASS MOLD

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.000
WITH A RELEASE AGENT.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.934
ONCE A RUBBER INSERT IS GLUED
INTO THE DRAIN HOLE,

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.100
A TECHNICIAN MIXES
THE INGREDIENTS

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.234
FOR THE CASTING MATERIAL
TOGETHER.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:59.701
INGREDIENTS INCLUDE PIGMENT
CONTAINING METAL OXIDES,

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:02.767
WHICH PREVENT COLOR FADING;
A CONCRETE MIX,

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:06.868
CONTAINING A BLEND OF FIBERS FOR
EXTRA STRENGTH AND RESISTANCE;

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:09.834
AND WATER CONTAINING
PROPRIETARY ADDITIVES.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:13.968
THE INGREDIENTS ARE MIXED
TOGETHER FOR ABOUT 3 MINUTES

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:18.033
UNTIL THE CONCRETE IS THE
CONSISTENCY OF CAKE BATTER.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:22.767
A THIN LAYERS IS SPRAYED ONTO
THE FIBERGLASS MOLD,

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:28.067
AND ANY RAISED AREAS ARE
FLATTENED TO REMOVE AIR BUBBLES.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.734
THE CHAIR'S COLOR WILL NEVER RUB
OFF FOR PEEL,

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:35.868
BECAUSE THE PIGMENT IS MIXED
RIGHT INTO THE CONCRETE.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.667
NEXT, TECHNICIANS ADD THE
HEATING ELEMENT --

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:41.968
A CABLE THAT IS WRAPPED AROUND
THE PIECE OF FURNITURE.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:46.234
THE CABLE IS TACKED IN PLACE
WITH A SEPARATE MIX OF CONCRETE

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.501
THAT HAS A HIGHER FIBER CONTENT.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:52.033
THE ENTIRE HEATING ELEMENT IS
EMBEDDED IN A FULL COAT

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.834
OF THE HIGH-FIBER CONCRETE.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.767
THEN A FINISHING COAT OF THE
FIRST MIX IS APPLIED.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.501
AND THE STRUCTURE
IS LEFT TO CURE

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.767
AT ROOM TEMPERATURE
FOR 24 HOURS.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.133
NOW CURED,
THIS WHITE CHAIR

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.100
IS READY TO BE EXTRACTED.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.000
A TECHNICIAN
PUMPS COMPRESSED AIR

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.100
THROUGH THE DRAIN-HOLE INSERT.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.367
DUE TO THE RELEASE AGENT
APPLICATION,

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:16.968
THE CAST CHAIR EASILY
POPS OFF THE MOLD.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:20.300
THE ROUGH EDGES ARE SMOOTHED
WITH A DIAMOND FILE.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:25.167
THEN THE DRAIN-HOLE PLUG
IS REMOVED.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:30.601
♪♪

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.968
AT ANOTHER STATION,
A TECHNICIAN COATS

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.934
THE ENTIRE SURFACE OF ANOTHER
CHAIR WITH A SEALANT

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.767
THAT BLOCKS MOISTURE.

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:40.701
MOISTURE PENETRATION
WEAKENS CONCRETE,

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:44.868
AND DRAWS OUT THE NATURAL SALT,
WHICH LEAVES WHITE STAINS.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:48.434
MEANWHILE, A WELDER CONSTRUCTS
THE CHAIR'S FRAME,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:52.434
WITH PARTS MADE OUT OF STAINLESS
STEEL TUBES AND PLATES.

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:55.534
THE CHAIR HAS THREE LEGS
PLUS CROSS MEMBERS

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:58.601
THAT ACT AS CONDUITS FOR
ELECTRICAL WIRES.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.701
THE CROSS MEMBERS CONNECT TO A
STAINLESS STEEL BOX,

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:04.501
WHICH WILL HOUSE THE
TEMPERATURE-CONTROL UNIT.

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:09.634
♪♪

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:12.701
A TECHNICIAN
FILLS A CHANNEL

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:16.300
WITH ADHESIVE
ALONG THE PERIMETER.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.234
HE PLACES THE FRAME
INTO THE CHANNEL.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:24.200
THE ADHESIVE
WILL TAKE A DAY TO CURE.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.901
NEXT, THE ELECTRICAL WIRING
IS ASSEMBLED.

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.434
THE TECHNICIAN FISHES TWO
ELECTRICAL WIRES

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.701
THROUGH THE FRAME,
ONE WIRE CONNECTS

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:34.968
THE POWER-CORD PLUG
TO THE TEMPERATURE CONTROL UNIT,

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:37.534
THE OTHER RUNS FROM THE
TEMPERATURE-CONTROL UNIT

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.467
TO THE
TEMPERATURE-CONTROL SWITCH.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:43.834
HE GLUES THE SWITCH INTO A HOLE
IN THE RIGHT FRONT LEG.

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.834
ALL THE WIRES
ARE EMBEDDED IN RUBBER,

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:48.334
MAKING THEM WATERPROOF.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:55.067
THE TEMPERATURE-CONTROL UNIT
IS INSTALLED IN THE BOX

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.067
AT THE CENTER OF THE FRAME.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:04:03.234
THEN A TEMPERATURE SENSOR IS
INSTALLED UNDERNEATH THE SEAT.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:06.834
THE TECHNICIAN HAMMERS PLASTIC
AND STAINLESS STEEL FEET

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.701
INTO THE BOTTOM OF THE LEGS.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:12.567
THIS PREVENTS THE LEGS FROM
SCRATCHING THE FLOOR

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:16.267
AND LEVELS THE FURNITURE ON AN
UNEVEN SURFACE.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:21.200
LASTLY, A BRONZE DRAIN IS
INSERTED INTO THE DRAIN HOLE.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.868
A QUALITY-CONTROLLED HEAT TEST
MEASURES THE SURFACE TEMPERATURE

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.601
WITH AN INFRARED THERMOMETER.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:32.567
IF ALL IS OPERATING CORRECTLY,
THE SENSOR UNDER THE SEAT

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:36.067
TELLS THE THERMOSTAT
AND THE TEMPERATURE-CONTROL UNIT

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.133
WHEN TO TURN THE HEAT ON OR OFF.

